            <ArticleTitle>Overlapping conditions in women with irritable bowel syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>25-30; quiz 31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Irritable bowel syndrome is a common and often unpredictable disorder with an increased incidence among women. It is characterized by abdominal pain associated with constipation-diarrhea. Recent research, current theories about etiology and pathophysiology, diagnosis, management, and overlapping conditions such as interstitial cystitis and chronic pelvic pain are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
